# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): arena.rs writes a table entry only
# through `store` (and `Arenas::put_entry`'s write of the atomic `new`
# made), heap/tcaches.rs only through `store` and `swap` (and
# `Tcaches::put_entry`'s write of the atomic `new` made), no other file
# calls these wrappers, and this file mints one EntryPerm per atomic, in
# `new` (tests/loom/tests/access.rs). C++20's coherence rules
# ([intro.races]) give a load the permission's value at its place in the
# entry's modification order. The arena table's stores are made under
# the creation lock, which orders them; the `Release` store and an
# `Acquire` load that reads it publish the arena `build` wrote (a
# release/acquire pair, [atomics.order] p2). The narenas model checks
# that on copies of the `Arenas` steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs). The
# tcache table's writes, `Tcaches::create`'s `Release` store and
# `Tcaches::destroy`'s `AcqRel` swap, are made under the table lock,
# which orders them; `create`'s store and a `Tcaches::get` `Acquire`
# load that reads it publish the heap `Heap::create_detached` built (the
# same pair). `destroy`'s swap is a read-modify-write, which reads the
# last value before its own write, for every ordering ([atomics.order]
# p10). No loom model runs the tcache table's steps. The GenMC narenas case
# runs `store` and `load` as they are over `core`'s `AtomicPtr<u64>`,
# inside pinned copies of the `Arenas` steps (tests/genmc/narenas.rs,
# `GENMC_PINS`), with the permissions erased, under RC11 only
# (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC"); no case runs the tcache table's steps.
store	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::entry_store, and loom: narenas::loom_narenas_create_publishes, and GenMC: narenas [rc11]; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the model runs as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configuration tests/loom/src/narenas.rs states, and beyond the configuration tests/genmc/narenas.rs states, which the GenMC case runs it in as it is over `core`'s atomic inside copies of the same steps, under RC11 only, which forbids load buffering (GenMC 0.20 stops on an internal check under IMM and ARMv8, tests/genmc/cases), and on the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build, and the tcache table's store in `Tcaches::create`, which no model or case runs, and `Arenas::put_arena0`'s store, which no case runs (the case starts with entry 0 published); the pointers' provenance (the harness compares addresses); the instances challoc uses, `T = Arena` and the tcache table's `T = u8` (checked at `T = u64`, as the GenMC case runs it); the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the entry's last write, which no GenMC case checks (the case erases the permissions, `Tracked::assume_new()`, so it sees no ghost value) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 1746040714, body 3052065581, spec 2813638883
load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::entry_load, and loom: narenas::loom_narenas_create_publishes, and GenMC: narenas [rc11]; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the model runs as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Arenas` steps, in the configuration tests/loom/src/narenas.rs states, and beyond the configuration tests/genmc/narenas.rs states, which the GenMC case runs it in as it is over `core`'s atomic inside copies of the same steps, under RC11 only, which forbids load buffering (GenMC 0.20 stops on an internal check under IMM and ARMv8, tests/genmc/cases), and on the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build, and the tcache table's load in `Tcaches::get`, which no model or case runs; the pointers' provenance (the harness compares addresses); the instances challoc uses, `T = Arena` and the tcache table's `T = u8` (checked at `T = u64`, as the GenMC case runs it); the C11 argument above, which no GenMC case checks (the case erases the permissions, `Tracked::assume_new()`, so it sees no ghost value) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3032578775, body 3163496896, spec 2813638883
# One atomic swap, as `core` documents; the permission carries the value.
swap	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::entry_swap; not checked: this body under concurrency, which no loom model runs (its one caller is `Tcaches::destroy`); the pointers' provenance (the harness compares addresses); the instance challoc uses, the tcache table's `T = u8` (checked at `T = u64`); the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the entry's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 1251989958, body 3908961486, spec 2813638883
